# Lepton 4-state group reconciliation: cyclotomic Z_4 ↔ Koide V_4 inside D_4

> **Question.** The repo carries two structurally inconsistent
> identifications of the 4-element group structure on N_lep = q_2² = 4
> lepton phase states:
> - The cyclotomic-content audits identify the 4 states with 4th
>   roots of unity {1, i, −1, −i}, labeling the group "Z_4 (Klein
>   four-group)" — math: Z_4 is cyclic of order 4, NOT the Klein
>   four-group.
> - The Koide-form audits identify the 4 states with phase symbols
>   {A, B, C, D} acted on by τ_2 (swaps A↔C, B↔D) and τ_3 (swaps
>   A↔B, C↔D), generating V_4 = Z_2 × Z_2 (the Klein four-group).
>
> These cannot both be the full picture: Z_4 and V_4 are
> non-isomorphic order-4 groups. Which one is the substrate-canonical
> structure on the lepton state set?

**Verdict: MODAL ✓ / GENERATIVE ✓** for the reconciliation. Both
identifications survive as *partial views* of the ambient symmetry
group **D_4** (dihedral group of the square, order 8 = q_2³). Z_4
is the rotation subgroup (cyclotomic labels via 4th roots of unity);
V_4 is the regular Klein-four subgroup ≤ A_4 (Koide's pair-swap
substrate action). They share the Z_2 center (180° rotation =
(AC)(BD)). Neither audit was wrong about its half; the disagreement
was in the union of the labels.

Class: foundational rigor check / structural reconciliation across
named substrate audits. Resolution-mode throughout — no apparatus
modification.

