## 2. Why both pictures are partial — and how they coexist

### Z_4 and V_4 are both order-4 subgroups of S_4 acting on {A, B, C, D}

Inside S_4 (the full permutation group on 4 elements), the two
subgroups are:
- **Z_4 = ⟨(ABCD)⟩** — the 4-cycle generated by the cyclic
  permutation (ABCD)
- **V_4 = {e, (AC)(BD), (AB)(CD), (AD)(BC)}** — the regular Klein
  four subgroup

Their intersection: (ABCD)² = (AC)(BD), which is τ_2. So **Z_4 ∩ V_4 =
{e, (AC)(BD)} ≅ Z_2** — the order-2 cyclic group generated by 180°
rotation.

Order of the join: |Z_4 · V_4| = |Z_4| · |V_4| / |Z_4 ∩ V_4| =
4 · 4 / 2 = **8**. So ⟨Z_4, V_4⟩ has order 8 in S_4.

### The ambient envelope is D_4

The order-8 subgroups of S_4 are the Sylow 2-subgroups (3 of them,
each isomorphic to D_4 = dihedral group of the square). Each contains
exactly one Z_4 and one regular V_4 as index-2 subgroups, with shared
Z_2 center.

So **⟨Z_4, V_4⟩ ≅ D_4** — the dihedral group of order 8.

Concretely, identifying {A, B, C, D} with the 4 vertices of a square
(equivalently, 4th roots of unity in ℂ):
- A = +1, B = +i, C = −1, D = −i
- D_4 = symmetry group of the square = {4 rotations} ∪ {4 reflections}
- **Z_4** = rotations: {identity, 90°, 180°, 270°}
- **V_4** (Koide) = {identity, 180°, reflection across y = x,
  reflection across y = −x} — the diagonal V_4 subgroup
- D_4 contains a *second* V_4 too: {identity, 180°, conjugation
  (real axis reflection), 180°+conjugation (imag axis reflection)}.
  This is NOT the Koide V_4; it acts non-regularly (each non-180°
  element fixes 2 of the 4 vertices). The Koide V_4 is the regular
  V_4 with no fixed points.

### What each subgroup carries

| Subgroup | Carrier | Substrate role |
|---|---|---|
| **Z_4** (rotations) | 4th roots of unity; cyclotomic Φ_4(x) = x² + 1 | **Labeling**: the 4 states inherit a cyclotomic Z_4 ordering from the q_2² = 4 substrate cardinality |
| **V_4** (Koide diagonal) | regular Klein-four action on {A,B,C,D} | **Action**: the substrate's τ_2, τ_3 involutions act on the 4 states without fixed points (regular V_4) |
| **Z_2 = ⟨180° rotation⟩** | shared center | **Shared structure**: τ_2 = (AC)(BD) appears in *both* Z_4 (as the square of the 4-cycle) and V_4 (as one of the three double-transpositions) |
| **D_4** (envelope) | full symmetry of the square / 4 vertices in ℂ | **Ambient**: order 8 = q_2³ — the framework-native cube of the Mihailescu q_2 prime |

### The reconciliation in one sentence

> The 4 lepton phase states sit at the vertices of a square in ℂ
> (4th roots of unity); the cyclotomic Z_4 labels the vertices via
> roots of Φ_4(x) = x² + 1, the Koide V_4 acts on the vertices by
> pair-swap involutions, and both subgroups live inside the ambient
> D_4 dihedral symmetry of order q_2³ = 8.

