## 5. Two pictures, one substrate

The cyclotomic-content audits and the Koide-form audits are not
contradicting each other; they are describing complementary aspects
of a single substrate structure:

| Audit family | Subgroup of D_4 | What it sees |
|---|---|---|
| Cyclotomic-content | Z_4 (rotations) | The state *labels* — cyclotomic content of q_2² = 4 via Φ_4(x); ordering of states by 4th roots of unity |
| Koide-form | V_4 (Koide diagonal) | The state *action* — substrate's two Z_2 involutions τ_2 (= half-twist about q_2 axis), τ_3 (= half-twist about q_3 axis), with τ_2 τ_3 = composite half-twist |
| Half-twist meta-structure (PR #240) | V_4 Z_2 generators | Each Z_2 generator of V_4 IS a half-twist; PR #240's eight half-twist instances are 4 of them at the lepton scale (the V_4 elements ×2 for both prime axes) |
| Cosmological Γ_0(6) (PR #242) | Klein-four W_6 | Atkin-Lehner involutions on modular-form cusps; a different (modular-surface-level) Klein four; NOT the same as the lepton-state V_4, but parallel structure at cosmological scale |
| W_6 invariance (PR #246, corrected) | W_6 Klein-four on cusps; cuspidal newform in trivial (+,+) W_6-irrep | Atkin-Lehner Klein four acts on Γ_0(6) cusps; f_{6,4} is invariant under all 4 elements |

The pattern across scales: the framework's natural 4-element group
structures appear in two forms — cyclic (cyclotomic, label-carrying)
or Klein-four (substrate action, involution-carrying) — and both are
present at most scales, sitting inside dihedral or Atkin-Lehner
envelopes. The audits that conflated "Z_4" with "Klein four-group"
were not seeing the conflation; they were correctly identifying *a*
4-element group at their scale but using imprecise terminology that
hid which one.

### What this resolves

- Cyclotomic-content audit's *cyclotomic Z_4 identification* is
  correct (just mis-labeled "Klein four-group")
- Koide-form audit's *V_4 substrate action* is correct
- Both coexist as subgroups of D_4
- The structural picture is *richer* than either audit alone — both
  cyclic and Klein content are simultaneously present

### What this does NOT change

- No substrate primitive added or removed; D_4 was already implicit
  in the framework via order 8 = q_2³ structure
- No cosmological prediction shifts; the Ω partition reading remains
- No Mihailescu primes shift; (q_2, q_3) = (2, 3) unchanged
- No empirical content changes; the audits' empirical readings
  (lepton mass ratios, etc.) are unaffected

